Kevin Brazos says, hi Sal,

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.920
where would you say your
optimism comes from?

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:07.370
I've always admired that presence in

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.480
your live streams and videos.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.960
Also, my background is
middle school science.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.968
I would love to help well, Kevin thanks.

00:18:11.968 --> 00:18:13.150
Thanks, (mummurs).

00:18:14.806 --> 00:18:16.310
I mean, look I think,

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.190
we all have a choice in life.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:20.453
Things are gonna happen to us for sure.

00:18:21.309 --> 00:18:23.490
And I consider myself lucky

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:25.290
that when you look at the whole spectrum

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.980
of the things that can
happen to you in life,

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.267
I've for the most part avoided

00:18:28.267 --> 00:18:31.970
most of the really bad ones knock on wood.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:34.520
But no matter what happens to you a lot,

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:37.703
depends on how you choose to look at it.

00:18:38.897 --> 00:18:40.040
There's the famous cliche,

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.485
is glass half full glass, half empty.

00:18:41.485 --> 00:18:46.485
And I have found that no
matter what life throws at you,

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.090
or at least those in me,

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:49.590
if I take it from a kind of

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:53.670
a more optimistic point of
view it's more productive,

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:54.690
it's more constructive

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.000
and it puts positive energy out there.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.080
I've said it in multiple times

00:18:58.080 --> 00:18:59.620
on this live stream

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.291
for students going to college and saying,

00:19:01.291 --> 00:19:02.590
I need to go to this college

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:03.560
or that college,

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.030
or I need to go into that career.

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:05.863
I was like,

00:19:05.863 --> 00:19:06.780
it's really what you put out there

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:08.100
that comes back regardless of

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:08.933
where you go to college

00:19:08.933 --> 00:19:09.766
or what you work in.

00:19:09.766 --> 00:19:11.205
If you put positive energy out there,

00:19:11.205 --> 00:19:12.520
if you have a sense of curiosity,

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.213
if you genuinely care about other people,

00:19:14.213 --> 00:19:18.890
then they will generally care about you.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.480
Things will be interesting.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.530
You will get a lot out of the experience.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:23.800
So I think when that clicks,

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:24.980
there's like, wow,

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:26.706
I should be optimistic.

00:19:26.706 --> 00:19:28.660
I'm sure you know, who knows?

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:29.493
I don't know how much of

00:19:29.493 --> 00:19:31.470
it is hard wired into folks.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:33.620
I would say in high school,

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.450
in certain circles I
was probably optimistic

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:36.580
and certain places I

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:37.740
was probably a little bit angry.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:38.870
I was probably a little bit angsty.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:39.703
I said in the past,

00:19:39.703 --> 00:19:42.100
I was the lead singer
of a heavy metal band.

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:43.700
And if I were to see some

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.056
of the lyrics that we,

00:19:45.056 --> 00:19:46.260
it probably would make,

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.110
in fact it would make me cringe today

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:50.410
because we were, I was angry.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:51.243
I was frustrated

00:19:51.243 --> 00:19:52.400
for who knows how much of

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.970
it was teenage angst.

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:56.120
How much was it just
context that I was in.

00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.144
But when I reflect on that,

00:19:59.144 --> 00:20:00.526
I realized that it's much,

00:20:00.526 --> 00:20:04.950
better to be not as angsty.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.433
It's a better way to approach the world.

00:20:07.433 --> 00:20:09.810
And the world kind of tends

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:12.170
to reflect that back when,

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.050
you do it.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.460
One piece of advice,

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:16.360
and I do this to myself all the time

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.210
is for smile.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:19.570
For smile, you might say like,

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.403
that seems forced,

00:20:20.403 --> 00:20:23.240
like literally like smile.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.750
But I actually have read research that,

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:25.750
just as if you're happy,

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:27.590
it makes you naturally smile.

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:28.423
It's almost hard not

00:20:28.423 --> 00:20:30.220
to smile if you're happy,

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:31.053
the other way around,

00:20:31.053 --> 00:20:32.343
if you force the smile,

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:36.000
that looks a little bit sinister,

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.594
that it can actually make you

00:20:37.594 --> 00:20:39.830
a little bit happier.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:40.905
So I've tried that,

00:20:40.905 --> 00:20:43.210
everyone who's watching try

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.043
to force a smile.

00:20:44.043 --> 00:20:44.980
I know there's a lot going on

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:45.813
in the world right now.

00:20:45.813 --> 00:20:47.870
That's stressful and should

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.293
not make any of us happy.

00:20:52.865 --> 00:20:54.540
It doesn't, help you

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:57.710
or the world to be down.

00:20:57.710 --> 00:20:59.180
We should always be kind of like,

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.478
Hey, look this is the data.

00:21:01.478 --> 00:21:03.607
This is what we have to deal with now.

00:21:03.607 --> 00:21:05.340
How can we put one foot in front

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.980
of the other to make positive change?

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:08.696
I think is always the question we should,

00:21:08.696 --> 00:21:09.860
be asking ourselves,

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:11.620
and we have this one life to live.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.620
And so as we try to make
that positive change,

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:14.560
even when we fail,

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:16.350
even when we get knocked down,

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.000
how do we live in the moment

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.330
and appreciate these moments we have to,

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:24.883
even sometimes fail and
make the most of it.

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:29.880
So, let's see, Elliot H.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:31.550
Says, Dumbledore Sal.

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:32.383
Well, thank you for calling

00:21:32.383 --> 00:21:33.640
that as many of y'all know,

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.250
I've always had the secret aspiration

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:38.063
to be a Dumbledore like figure one day.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:39.970
Did you always have

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:43.980
a Buddhist flesh, Hindu
detached philosophy?

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:45.180
When did you start forcing yourself

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:46.570
to smile and enjoy the process

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.770
rather than frown
worrying about the result?

00:21:50.371 --> 00:21:51.740
It's interesting. I mean,

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:52.680
a lot of these ideas

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:55.570
are often associated with
Eastern philosophies,

00:21:55.570 --> 00:21:58.530
like Buddhist, Hindu, Vedas philosophies.

00:21:58.530 --> 00:21:59.363
But if you look

00:21:59.363 --> 00:22:02.430
at almost any philosophical system,

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:05.200
even many from the West Stoicism famously,

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:07.480
from the Greeks and the Romans,

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:09.960
it's essentially the same general idea

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:13.811
of not becoming attached to the outcome

00:22:13.811 --> 00:22:17.160
and really just doing what is right.

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:18.454
Not only will you be

00:22:18.454 --> 00:22:21.610
in some ways a better human being,

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:22.443
but you're also going

00:22:22.443 --> 00:22:23.640
to be a happier human being,

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:25.250
a more peaceful human being.

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:26.170
And if you look at some of

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:27.970
the especially the mystical traditions

00:22:27.970 --> 00:22:29.220
and some of them,

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:31.630
the major religion,

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:34.140
when you look at the Sufi traditions,

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:35.390
you look at Gnosticism

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:37.880
and Christianity there's definitely

00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:40.224
the mystical traditions in Judaism.

00:22:40.224 --> 00:22:43.290
They also, kind of go into some

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:44.458
of these same ideas.

00:22:44.458 --> 00:22:47.270
In Hebrew, the word sin,

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.570
we have this notion that sin is,

00:22:49.570 --> 00:22:50.570
when you go against

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.040
the laws of the divine laws

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:54.670
or however you want to define it.

00:22:54.670 --> 00:22:56.630
But the original meaning

00:22:56.630 --> 00:22:58.860
of sin is to miss the point.

00:22:58.860 --> 00:23:01.250
And there are interpretations

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:02.474
of many religions where,

00:23:02.474 --> 00:23:04.560
notions of evil

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:07.852
are much more about getting sucked,

00:23:07.852 --> 00:23:12.852
into the illusion of power

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:16.580
and materiality and,

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:18.500
comparing yourself to others

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:21.808
and, status and

00:23:21.808 --> 00:23:23.308
that almost constructs,

00:23:23.308 --> 00:23:25.170
not to get too philosophical,

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:26.100
but that almost constructs

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:29.100
a hell of it in its own sort in your mind.

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:30.200
'Cause that obsession,

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.370
that anxiety over,

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:33.420
keeping up with others,

00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:34.650
comparing to others.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:36.470
I'm not where I should be.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:37.590
I wanna be richer.

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:38.620
I wanna be more powerful.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:39.560
I wanna be better looking.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.067
I wanna have better things.

00:23:41.067 --> 00:23:43.970
That missing the point

00:23:43.970 --> 00:23:46.840
almost creates a form of a hell,

00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:48.590
even in your own mind.

00:23:48.590 --> 00:23:49.423
So I think this is actually

00:23:49.423 --> 00:23:50.460
a thread that exists

00:23:50.460 --> 00:23:54.580
throughout pretty much
any religious tradition

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:56.150
or any philosophical system,

00:23:56.150 --> 00:23:57.397
like the Stoics.

00:23:58.590 --> 00:24:01.830
I think I kind of personally,

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:02.850
stumbled into this.

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:03.970
I've always been intrigued

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:06.010
by making sense of the universe

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:07.192
that we live in.

00:24:07.192 --> 00:24:09.310
I think it was really,

00:24:09.310 --> 00:24:11.520
when you were a teenager that you really,

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:13.180
a lot of teenagers out there think that,

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:15.690
okay, people who are 50, 60, 70,

00:24:15.690 --> 00:24:17.840
or 80 years old must be
way deeper than I am,

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:18.980
because they've had so much more time

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:20.100
to think about it.

00:24:20.100 --> 00:24:21.170
But I think,

00:24:21.170 --> 00:24:22.230
it's actually in middle schoolers

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:23.063
and teenagers that

00:24:23.063 --> 00:24:23.896
are the ones that

00:24:23.896 --> 00:24:24.850
are oftentimes the thinking

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:27.490
the most deeply about some of these.

00:24:27.490 --> 00:24:28.730
Like, why do we exist?

00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:29.563
Why am I here?

00:24:29.563 --> 00:24:30.960
What's the purpose of life?

00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:31.960
And then when all this happens,

00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:32.793
you go to college,

00:24:32.793 --> 00:24:33.626
you get a job,

00:24:33.626 --> 00:24:34.459
you have a family.

00:24:34.459 --> 00:24:35.292
And you're just like,

00:24:35.292 --> 00:24:36.125
okay, I got to pay my mortgage.

00:24:36.125 --> 00:24:38.040
I got to make sure my
kids learn how to swim.

00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:40.650
I got to have all these social gatherings.

00:24:40.650 --> 00:24:42.920
I got to make sure that
I get that promotion.

00:24:42.920 --> 00:24:44.086
And so actually I think a lot of adults,

00:24:44.086 --> 00:24:46.780
have, almost that muscle

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:47.660
of thinking deeply

00:24:47.660 --> 00:24:49.260
about the universe we live in,

00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:51.800
and what it means to be a good person,

00:24:51.800 --> 00:24:54.193
et cetera, oftentimes atrophies.

00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:57.680
So anyway, to answer your question,

00:24:57.680 --> 00:24:59.210
probably in middle school,

00:24:59.210 --> 00:25:01.050
I was drawn to some of these things

00:25:01.050 --> 00:25:02.500
and I continue to be,

00:25:02.500 --> 00:25:04.833
and I think now that I'm middle aged,

00:25:06.491 --> 00:25:08.600
and I realized that,

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:11.790
the time goes by very fast in life.

00:25:11.790 --> 00:25:13.840
It feels like just
yesterday I was in college,

00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:15.790
but that's literally 20 years ago.

00:25:15.790 --> 00:25:17.160
And another 20 years

00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:18.780
I'm going to be in well into my sixties.

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:19.820
And another 20 years of that,

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:20.899
if I'm lucky,

00:25:20.899 --> 00:25:23.328
I may or may not be around.

00:25:23.328 --> 00:25:25.093
And so I think it is,

00:25:27.432 --> 00:25:28.783
a lot of times people think

00:25:28.783 --> 00:25:30.160
it's a distraction to think

00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:31.330
about these philosophical ideas

00:25:31.330 --> 00:25:32.770
or our purpose in life,

00:25:32.770 --> 00:25:36.140
or, how we fit into the cosmos or,

00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:38.040
the nature of however
you wanna to view it,

00:25:38.040 --> 00:25:39.460
God, the universe.

00:25:39.460 --> 00:25:40.960
But I don't think it's ever too early

00:25:40.960 --> 00:25:41.793
to think about that.

00:25:41.793 --> 00:25:43.470
If anything, a lot of the other things

00:25:43.470 --> 00:25:47.050
we have in our life is
a distraction from that.

00:25:47.050 --> 00:25:48.220
There's, I forgot who said it,

00:25:48.220 --> 00:25:50.610
I forgot which philosophical
system it came out of.

00:25:50.610 --> 00:25:52.410
But, when you meditate and you still,

00:25:52.410 --> 00:25:53.910
your mind, it's much more about,

00:25:53.910 --> 00:25:57.670
it's not about forgetting
your kind of problems.

00:25:57.670 --> 00:25:59.860
It's more about remembering
what you really are,

00:25:59.860 --> 00:26:03.280
that you aren't defined just by your name,

00:26:03.280 --> 00:26:05.760
your persona, your gender,

00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:07.330
your status in the world,

00:26:07.330 --> 00:26:08.610
your education, all of these things

00:26:08.610 --> 00:26:10.720
that frankly are egos identify

00:26:10.720 --> 00:26:12.040
very strongly with.

00:26:12.040 --> 00:26:14.140
But when you really stole your mind,

00:26:14.140 --> 00:26:15.810
you realize that you're in awareness

00:26:15.810 --> 00:26:17.430
and that's all you really know.

00:26:17.430 --> 00:26:20.320
And that when you kind of strip away,

00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:21.400
some of those other things,

00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:23.130
it can give you peace

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:24.930
and clarity on a lot of levels,

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:27.670
but not just kind of at a spiritual level,

00:26:27.670 --> 00:26:29.990
but to engage with the world as a whole.

00:26:29.990 --> 00:26:31.040
But anyway, I'll get off

00:26:31.040 --> 00:26:35.453
of my soap box on philosophy.

00:26:37.570 --> 00:26:39.030
John Corley from Facebook says,

00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:41.040
you are aging Sal just like me,

00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:43.520
silver Fox, unlike me.

00:26:43.520 --> 00:26:44.840
Yes, I guess I am.

00:26:44.840 --> 00:26:45.673
I have to say,

00:26:45.673 --> 00:26:47.470
all this high-minded talk

00:26:47.470 --> 00:26:50.930
about not being having vanity

00:26:50.930 --> 00:26:53.083
and not being connected,

00:26:53.083 --> 00:26:55.130
not letting your ego run.

00:26:55.130 --> 00:26:57.290
There is something that
hit me when I hit 40.

00:26:57.290 --> 00:26:58.260
I'm now 43.

00:26:58.260 --> 00:26:59.093
You're gonna hit,

00:26:59.093 --> 00:27:01.184
be 44 where it was.

00:27:01.184 --> 00:27:04.620
It didn't hit my wife as bad.

00:27:04.620 --> 00:27:05.453
It hit me

00:27:05.453 --> 00:27:06.880
and maybe maybe I do have more vanity

00:27:06.880 --> 00:27:08.470
than I'd like to admit,

00:27:08.470 --> 00:27:09.619
but it was that realization,

00:27:09.619 --> 00:27:13.630
that my wife and I had
been married 16 years.

00:27:13.630 --> 00:27:14.860
And when we got married,

00:27:14.860 --> 00:27:15.901
we were in their twenties where,

00:27:15.901 --> 00:27:19.100
we're young, 16 years kind
of went by super fast.

00:27:19.100 --> 00:27:19.933
I think that's a reflection

00:27:19.933 --> 00:27:21.050
of my wife being a,

00:27:21.050 --> 00:27:22.590
or mama, being a,

00:27:22.590 --> 00:27:24.757
a wonderful person to share a life with.

00:27:24.757 --> 00:27:25.590
And I'm like,

00:27:25.590 --> 00:27:26.423
wait, another 16 years,

00:27:26.423 --> 00:27:27.570
I'm going to be 60.

00:27:27.570 --> 00:27:30.065
60 is like, I never imagined myself.

00:27:30.065 --> 00:27:32.148
(laughs)

00:27:33.170 --> 00:27:34.480
And so, yeah, no,

00:27:34.480 --> 00:27:36.840
there is something about aging that,

00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:38.270
that definitely starts to hit you.

00:27:38.270 --> 00:27:39.431
At least hit me when I'm 40.

00:27:39.431 --> 00:27:42.500
And and yeah, but we're,

00:27:42.500 --> 00:27:43.642
we're all aging,

00:27:43.642 --> 00:27:45.360
the beard isn't helping

00:27:45.360 --> 00:27:47.520
'cause my beard is grayer than normal,

00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:50.085
but I'm resisting any temptations

00:27:50.085 --> 00:27:53.380
to use any dyes or anything

00:27:53.380 --> 00:27:55.160
to try to be something that I'm not,

00:27:55.160 --> 00:27:56.630
but I'm sure those words will come

00:27:56.630 --> 00:27:57.910
to bite me back when I show up

00:27:57.910 --> 00:27:58.790
on this live stream

00:27:58.790 --> 00:28:01.939
with jet black beard in a few weeks.

00:28:01.939 --> 00:28:04.160
(laughs)

00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:05.160
I see we have maybe a time

00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:07.933
for one or two more questions.

00:28:08.986 --> 00:28:13.263
Let's see, Attara Lapet
asks from Facebook.

00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:18.880
How would I maintain mastery

00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:20.450
based learning in university?

00:28:20.450 --> 00:28:21.283
What I would say

00:28:21.283 --> 00:28:22.680
when you learn things in university,

00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:23.850
don't just cram for the test.

00:28:23.850 --> 00:28:25.070
Yes. Try to get good grades.

00:28:25.070 --> 00:28:26.300
And if you need a cram sometimes,

00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:28.110
'cause you kind of let
things slide a little bit,

00:28:28.110 --> 00:28:30.700
do that, but always review it

00:28:30.700 --> 00:28:32.670
and learn and try to learn for mastery.

00:28:32.670 --> 00:28:33.503
And if you do that,

00:28:33.503 --> 00:28:34.619
what you're gonna find is,

00:28:34.619 --> 00:28:36.260
if you really master

00:28:36.260 --> 00:28:38.790
those introductory courses in college,

00:28:38.790 --> 00:28:39.700
the rest of the course

00:28:39.700 --> 00:28:41.410
actually ended up pretty intuitive.

00:28:41.410 --> 00:28:42.400
If you don't master

00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:44.300
those introductory courses in college,

00:28:44.300 --> 00:28:45.133
the rest of the courses

00:28:45.133 --> 00:28:46.320
in college are gonna continue

00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:47.190
to be a struggle

00:28:47.190 --> 00:28:48.620
and you're gonna continue to have to cram.

00:28:48.620 --> 00:28:49.460
And you feel like

00:28:49.460 --> 00:28:50.680
you're not really learning anything.

00:28:50.680 --> 00:28:51.700
So I would say,

00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:54.640
especially those introductory courses

00:28:54.640 --> 00:28:56.990
get really deep mastery of them.

00:28:56.990 --> 00:28:58.360
And then you'll be pretty unstoppable.

00:28:58.360 --> 00:29:00.770
I mean, I know people with PhDs in biology

00:29:00.770 --> 00:29:04.060
and they'll tell you,

00:29:04.060 --> 00:29:05.440
if you really master

00:29:05.440 --> 00:29:06.794
that first year biology course,

00:29:06.794 --> 00:29:09.850
you can have a very deep conversation

00:29:09.850 --> 00:29:11.950
with them or with your professors

00:29:11.950 --> 00:29:13.020
or whoever else.

00:29:13.020 --> 00:29:14.993
That's my best advice.

00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:16.760
Maybe one more question,

00:29:16.760 --> 00:29:18.310
Tina Lou, do you like teaching?

00:29:19.370 --> 00:29:20.420
Yeah. I mean, if it's not obvious,

00:29:20.420 --> 00:29:21.357
I love it.

00:29:21.357 --> 00:29:24.163
I consider myself very fortunate because,

00:29:25.526 --> 00:29:29.690
to be able to have the opportunity

00:29:29.690 --> 00:29:30.910
to learn material

00:29:30.910 --> 00:29:32.270
in the non-stressful way

00:29:32.270 --> 00:29:34.020
where I'm not being evaluated,

00:29:34.020 --> 00:29:35.940
but I can just learn it
for the sake of learning,

00:29:35.940 --> 00:29:37.700
but then have a reason for learning it,

00:29:37.700 --> 00:29:41.270
so that I can digested in my own mind

00:29:41.270 --> 00:29:43.860
and then help other people
get to the same place.

00:29:43.860 --> 00:29:46.033
I think it's a incredibly powerful thing.

00:29:46.033 --> 00:29:47.650
And I remember when I was

00:29:47.650 --> 00:29:50.893
a kid reading textbooks from,

00:29:51.770 --> 00:29:53.030
some great thinkers,

00:29:53.030 --> 00:29:53.970
so to speak,

00:29:53.970 --> 00:29:54.850
there's a certain connection

00:29:54.850 --> 00:29:56.010
that you form across time

00:29:56.010 --> 00:29:56.860
and space when you're able

00:29:56.860 --> 00:29:57.760
to go really deep

00:29:57.760 --> 00:29:58.940
and especially intellectual

00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:00.700
or philosophical subjects.

00:30:00.700 --> 00:30:02.840
And, I feel very privileged

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:05.100
and very lucky that hopefully,

00:30:05.100 --> 00:30:05.933
I can help.

00:30:05.933 --> 00:30:06.810
And the Khan Academy team

00:30:06.810 --> 00:30:08.730
can help form those same connections

00:30:08.730 --> 00:30:09.563
with people that we might

00:30:09.563 --> 00:30:11.420
not know across time and space.

00:30:11.420 --> 00:30:13.250
There might be some young girl

00:30:13.250 --> 00:30:15.500
in the village someplace in 300 years and

00:30:15.500 --> 00:30:17.210
hopefully Khan Academy still around

00:30:17.210 --> 00:30:18.700
and maybe some of our existing content

00:30:18.700 --> 00:30:21.270
is hopefully still useful for her.

00:30:21.270 --> 00:30:22.450
And she's just like, Oh, wow.

00:30:22.450 --> 00:30:25.192
I feel connection with
these folks back in,

00:30:25.192 --> 00:30:27.910
the 21st century.

00:30:27.910 --> 00:30:28.990
I think there's just something

00:30:28.990 --> 00:30:30.000
really cool about that.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.540
And as I was just saying,

00:30:32.540 --> 00:30:34.840
we're in this puzzle called life

00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:35.770
and to understand it

00:30:35.770 --> 00:30:37.540
and learning new things

00:30:37.540 --> 00:30:39.400
is the best way I can think of,

00:30:39.400 --> 00:30:41.980
really trying to make
sense of this puzzle,

00:30:41.980 --> 00:30:43.840
where in, this universe we're in

00:30:45.060 --> 00:30:46.240
and our purpose

00:30:46.240 --> 00:30:49.140
in the fairly limited time that we have.

00:30:49.140 --> 00:30:50.270
So I'll let everyone go.

00:30:50.270 --> 00:30:52.220
I got a little bit more philosophical,

00:30:52.220 --> 00:30:54.470
maybe what's going on

00:30:54.470 --> 00:30:55.422
in the world is making maybe,

00:30:55.422 --> 00:30:58.123
all of us a little bit
more philosophical now.

00:31:01.060 --> 00:31:02.460
I pride myself to Khan Academy

00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:04.110
where we're we're nonpolitical.

00:31:04.110 --> 00:31:07.310
We definitely, I try to keep,

00:31:07.310 --> 00:31:09.030
any kind of clear religious

00:31:09.030 --> 00:31:10.530
or spiritual beliefs to myself

00:31:10.530 --> 00:31:13.670
'cause we're not about condoning one,

00:31:13.670 --> 00:31:14.902
one side or anything,

00:31:14.902 --> 00:31:17.620
one spiritual viewer and others.

00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:19.390
I hope I didn't cross any lines.

00:31:19.390 --> 00:31:22.150
But I just want to thank
everyone for joining.

00:31:22.150 --> 00:31:22.983
And as always,

00:31:22.983 --> 00:31:23.816
I enjoyed this

00:31:23.816 --> 00:31:25.840
and, these really stressful times,

00:31:25.840 --> 00:31:27.890
obviously you have everything going

00:31:27.890 --> 00:31:29.953
on in the US which is,

00:31:34.810 --> 00:31:35.643
I'm trying to pick between

00:31:35.643 --> 00:31:36.960
the word fortunate or unfortunate.

00:31:36.960 --> 00:31:38.232
It's good that finally,

00:31:38.232 --> 00:31:39.550
it feels like

00:31:39.550 --> 00:31:41.620
there's energy behind making change.

00:31:41.620 --> 00:31:43.110
Obviously, the unfortunate thing

00:31:43.110 --> 00:31:44.240
is the context that

00:31:44.240 --> 00:31:46.870
are forcing folks to,

00:31:46.870 --> 00:31:48.950
have to take a lot of action here,

00:31:48.950 --> 00:31:50.600
but between that

00:31:50.600 --> 00:31:52.870
and obviously what's
going on with COVID-19

00:31:52.870 --> 00:31:53.960
and being socially distant.

00:31:53.960 --> 00:31:56.180
I know it's a hard time
for a lot, of folks.

00:31:56.180 --> 00:31:57.587
So just encourage you yourself.

00:31:57.587 --> 00:32:00.470
Don't, take it easy on yourself.

00:32:00.470 --> 00:32:02.500
No matter what life stage you are in

00:32:03.612 --> 00:32:04.720
and try to enjoy the moment,

00:32:04.720 --> 00:32:07.000
give yourself some moments of stillness.

00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:08.880
I try to force a smile every now and then,

00:32:08.880 --> 00:32:09.740
and hopefully those smiles

00:32:09.740 --> 00:32:12.660
become a little bit more
automatic and normal.

00:32:12.660 --> 00:32:15.203
And I will see all of y'all on Monday.

